            description="Processing mode boundary. DETERMINISTIC steps are mechanical operations (reading input, writing output, validating schema) where the LLM must follow exact procedures with no creativity. PROBABILISTIC steps require LLM intelligence (rewriting text, making quality judgments, creative decisions). The transformer uses mode declarations to compile different prompt patterns for each step type.\nProcessing mode boundary. 'deterministic' steps are mechanical operations where the LLM must follow exact procedures. 'probabilistic' steps require LLM intelligence for creative or evaluative work.",
